From 093b6fd86be2fd28887bcb9ba9008ac97019dc61 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: NeoTech <andreas@roughedge.se>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 14:33:38 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] fix(sim): judge radial rapids against the raw stock
 instead of standing the law down

Law (d) stood down for Mode::Radial (M5.2 F2): the column reading cannot
see a horizontal bore, so the kernel's traverse promise was trusted and a
cross-drill rapid through uncut stock posted silently (#77's shape).

Radial programs now get a solid reading (verify/rapids_radial.rs): the
posed flute body, sampled under the modal pose rule, against the stock
prism minus the kerf the earlier cuts swept. A rapid through stock reads
RapidInStock and blocks the post; retracts up a just-drilled hole and peck
chip breaks ride their own kerf and stay clean.

drilling_cross's 44 mm box fixture is a real #77 collision on main (the
approach stops inside the raw box): the clean-document test runs on a
bar-sized stock, and a new test pins that the box document never posts
silently.

Fixes #79

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
